                        "glosses": [
                            "A hypertrophic skin disorder characterised by rough, dry, thickened skin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d13f0d3-2da9-4cc8-81a7-a0477cdfca45",
                                "sense_id": "fd1c8397-10bd-3da4-87d9-3105c6d87d0c",
                                "text": "As an inordinate production of epidermis dependent on hypertrophy of the papillæ of the skin, it has a title to a place in this group, while its principal character, namly, that of thickening and condensation of the skin, seems to point to pachylosis (καχὸς, crassitudo) as a fitting description."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d67ef65a-9294-4efc-bde6-0b836287093c",
                                "sense_id": "fd1c8397-10bd-3da4-87d9-3105c6d87d0c",
                                "text": "The majority of them had capillaries dilatation with pigmentation spots. The skin texture of some patients had subtle changes like pachylosis and deepened dermatoglyph, which were invisible for naked eyes."
                            }
                        ]
